switching gears now from fires to  natural disasters even delivering blood  the red cross is always on the lookout  for more volunteers now they're honoring  a dozen of them encouraging everyone to  donate volunteer give blood or take a  life-saving class  the red cross is known around the globe  for the assistance it provides often in  the most dire circumstances every year  chapters across the country including  southern nevada's recognize 12  distinguished volunteers it's no easy  task according to executive director  rachel flanagan we could not do what we  do without them they actually make up  more than 90 percent of our workforce  southern nevada's chapter has 628  volunteers during a virtual ceremony the  american red cross honored these 12  individuals for their commitment to  responding during the past year's  destructive wildfire season supporting  disaster relief nationwide and  responding to local home fires  delivering services all while navigating  the worldwide pandemic people like stan  smith the board chairman he championed  our recent battle of the badge's blood  drive which brought in 176 units of  blood in one day nikki morachnik had  more than 3 300 hours of on-call time  she responds to fires all over the  valley and makes people feel absolutely  incredible and she's done this year over  year over year  the red cross looking for additional  volunteers people willing to come out  and train and respond on fires like  nikki and the agency is also looking for  folks to deliver blood to 10 area  hospitals that is a constant need you  can set that up dependent upon your own  schedule to learn more about  volunteering at the american red cross  go to our website at eight newsnow dot  com we have a link set up for you
 

